o offense and as  opposed to nation building look we're  building roads  schools bridges highways and hospitals  half a world away and don't we have  those same needs here in this country  what about Medicaid Medicaid as the  country's health plan for the poor its  split between the federal government and  states so you're just saying poor people  you're on your own so as governor of New  Mexico I oversaw the reform of Medicaid  we took it from health care to the poor  we took it from a fee-for-service model  to a managed care model so we bet with  set up better healthcare networks and we  saved hundreds of millions of dollars  Nick at the time I believe that if the  federal government would have blocked  granted the state of New Mexico  forty-three percent less money for  Medicaid done away with all the strings  and the mandates associated on the  delivery of healthcare to the poor that  I could have effectively overseen the  delivery of healthcare to the poor no  strings no mandates fixed amount of  money I think the same template needs to  apply to Medicare health care for those  over 65 federal government Block Grant  the states federal government get out of  the business of health care delivery  completely and leave it up to 50  laboratories of innovation and best  practice and I think that's exactly what  you'll have fabulous success that will  get emulated by other states horrible  failure that will get avoided for the  same reasons one of the goals of your  candidacy is to make sure that you get  on the debate stage with Mitt Romney and  with Barack Obama what what has to  happen for that to happen and what are  you doing to make that well right right  now I need to be in the polls that  determine who gets in the debates now in  the polls that I'm in I'm at a low of  six percent I'm at a high of fifteen  percent so that's saying likely voters  when they're saying hey who you going to  vote for for president Gary Johnson  shown up somewhere between six to six  percent and 15 when my name is included  so right now we're asking everybody I'm  asking everybody that would be watching  this get online Gary Johnson 2012 and  and we have a list of the phone numbers  of all the polling organizations just  ask the polling organizations to include  my name in the polls you have a  fascinating  a succinct campaign slogan right now  which revolves around the idea of saying  vote libertarian just this one time and  I'm mangling it but what's the thinking  behind that and what do you what are you  hoping to work out that that there are a  lot more people in this country that  describe themselves as libertarian than  vote libertarian so what we're trying to  tie into here is just that notion look  you are a libertarian you're a  libertarian so how about voting that way  and by libertarian you mean fiscally  conservative socially liberal speaking  with a broad brush stroke yeah we're  Fisk that we are fiscally responsible  and that we actually care about really  care about civil liberties and the  erosion of those civil liberties so yeah  you're a libertarian but how about just  this one time voting that way and what  will that accomplish me being in the  White House and I'm gonna argue actually  addressing the problems that we have in  this country yeah okay well governor  gary johnson thank you very much the  Libertarian Party candidate for  president in 2012 thanks for talking  with reason to go thank you very much  for reason TV I'm Nick Gillespie
 

